.TH QT 1
.SH NAME
qt \- Quicktable command-line client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qt
[
.B -addr
.I url
] [
.B -token
.I token
]
.I command
[
.I arg ...
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Qt
talks to a Quicktable server over its REST API.
Each invocation runs one
.I command
against the server at
.IR url ,
by default
.BR http://localhost:16000 .
.PP
Results are written to standard output:
values, rows and query results as indented JSON;
table names and row keys as plain lines of text.
Commands that only modify state print nothing.
Diagnostics go to standard error.
.PP
Arguments named
.I json-*
must be a single JSON document,
so quote them for the shell.
The
.B -addr
and
.B -token
flags must precede the command.
.PP
Every request carries
.I token
as a bearer token,
which must match the token the server was started with.
Prefer setting
.B QUICKTABLE_TOKEN
over
.BR -token :
command-line arguments are visible to other users in the process list.
.SS Server
.TP
.B health
Exit 0 if the server is up and answering requests, 1 otherwise.
Needs no token.
.SS Tables
.TP
.B list-tables
Print the name of every table, one per line, sorted.
.TP
.BI drop-table " table"
Delete
.I table
and all its rows.
Dropping a table that does not exist is not an error.
.TP
.BI list-columns " table"
Print the name of every column used by any row of
.IR table ,
one per line, sorted.
This scans every key of the table.
.SS Cells
.TP
.BI get-cell " table rowkey column"
Print the value of one cell.
.TP
.BI set-cell " table rowkey column json-value"
Set one cell to
.IR json-value ,
a JSON number, string or boolean:
.BR 42 ,
.BR '"text"' ,
.BR true .
Arrays, objects and
.B null
are rejected.
.TP
.BI del-cell " table rowkey column"
Remove one cell.
.SS Rows
.TP
.BI list-rows " table"
Print the key of every row in
.IR table ,
one per line, sorted.
Listing a table that does not exist prints nothing.
.TP
.BI get-row " table rowkey"
Print all columns of a row as a JSON object.
.TP
.BI get-cells " table rowkey column \fR...\fP"
Print the named columns of a row as a JSON object.
Columns the row does not have are left out;
a row that does not exist prints
.BR {} .
.TP
.BI row-exists " table rowkey"
Print
.B true
if the row holds any cell,
.B false
otherwise.
.TP
.BI set-row " table rowkey json-columns"
Merge the columns of the JSON object
.I json-columns
into the row.
Columns not named are left alone.
.TP
.BI insert-row " table \fR[\fPjson-columns\fR]"
Create a row with a server-generated, unused key and print the key.
Without
.I json-columns
only the key is printed:
a row exists only while it holds a cell.
.TP
.BI del-row " table rowkey"
Remove a row.
.SS Queries
.TP
.BI query " table \fR[\fPjson-query\fR]"
Scan
.I table
and print a JSON object with fields
.BR table ,
.B rows
(each with
.B rowKey
and
.BR columns )
and
.BR count .
Without
.I json-query
all rows are returned.
.I Json-query
is an object with any of the fields:
.RS
.TP
.B prefix
string; only keys with this prefix.
.TP
.B startKey
string; first key of the range.
.TP
.B endKey
string; end of the range.
.TP
.B select
array of column names to return.
.TP
.B orderDesc
boolean; scan in descending key order.
.TP
.B offset
number of matching rows to skip.
.TP
.B limit
maximum number of rows to return.
.TP
.B where
array of predicates
.BR "{\(dqcolumn\(dq: \fIname\fP, \(dqop\(dq: \fIop\fP, \(dqvalue\(dq: \fIv\fP}" ,
all of which must hold.
.TP
.B or
array of predicate arrays;
a row matches if all predicates of any array hold.
Cannot be combined with
.BR where .
.TP
.B countOnly
boolean; return only
.BR count .
With
.B countOnly
only
.B count
is printed.
.TP
.B aggregate
column name; print only an object with the
.BR count ,
.BR sum ,
.BR min ,
.B max
and
.B avg
of the numeric values of that column in matching rows.
Rows where it is missing or not a number are skipped,
and
.B offset
and
.B limit
are ignored.
Cannot be combined with
.BR countOnly .
.RE
.TP
.BI del-query " table json-filter"
Delete every row of
.I table
matching
.I json-filter
in one transaction and print how many were deleted.
.I Json-filter
takes the fields of
.I json-query
except
.BR select ,
.B countOnly
and
.BR aggregate ;
.B offset
and
.B limit
apply as in
.BR query .
Unknown keys are rejected,
so a misspelled
.B where
never deletes every row;
.B {}
deletes every row.
.SS Batches
.TP
.BI batch-get " table key \fR...\fP"
Print a JSON object mapping each key to its row.
.TP
.BI batch-write " table json-mutations"
Apply a JSON array of mutations in one transaction:
all succeed or none do.
Each mutation is an object with
.B rowKey
and any of
.B setCols
(object of columns to set),
.B delCols
(array of columns to delete first)
and
.B delete
(true removes the whole row).
Unknown keys are rejected.
.TP
.BI batch-delete " table key \fR...\fP"
Delete every named row.
.TP
.BI batch-insert " table json-rows"
Insert a JSON array of row objects in one transaction,
each under a new server-generated key,
and print the keys one per line in the order of the rows.
.SS Atomic operations
.TP
.BI incr " table rowkey column delta"
Add the JSON number
.I delta
to a numeric cell and print the new value.
.TP
.BI append " table rowkey column value"
Append
.I value
to a string cell and print the new value.
.I Value
is taken literally, not as JSON.
.TP
.BI prepend " table rowkey column value"
As
.BR append ,
but at the front.
.TP
.BI cas " table rowkey json-body"
Check and set.
.I Json-body
is
.BR "{\(dqcondition\(dq: \fIcond\fP, \(dqsetCols\(dq: \fIcolumns\fP}" ,
where
.I cond
is
.BR "{\(dqcolumn\(dq: \fIname\fP, \(dqop\(dq: \fIop\fP, \(dqvalue\(dq: \fIv\fP}" .
If the condition holds, the columns in
.I columns
are written to the row atomically.
Without a condition the write is unconditional.
Keys match regardless of case;
unknown keys are rejected,
so a misspelled
.B condition
never becomes an unconditional write.
.TP
.BI cad " table rowkey json-body"
Check and delete.
.I Json-body
is
.BR "{\(dqcondition\(dq: \fIcond\fP, \(dqdelCols\(dq: \fIcolumns\fP}" ,
with
.I cond
as in
.BR cas .
If the condition holds, the columns named in the array
.I columns
are deleted atomically,
or the whole row if
.B delCols
is absent.
Without a condition the delete is unconditional.
Unknown keys are rejected,
so a misspelled
.B delCols
never deletes the whole row.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QUICKTABLE_ADDR
Default server address;
.B -addr
overrides it.
.TP
.B QUICKTABLE_TOKEN
Default bearer token;
.B -token
overrides it.
.SH EXAMPLES
Store and read back a counter:
.IP
.EX
qt set-cell stats 00000001 hits 0
qt incr stats 00000001 hits 1
qt get-cell stats 00000001 hits
.EE
.PP
Insert a user and list the names of the first ten adults whose key starts with
.BR a :
.IP
.EX
qt insert-row users '{"name": "ann", "age": 31}'
qt query users '{"prefix": "a", "limit": 10, "select": ["name"],
	"where": [{"column": "age", "op": ">=", "value": 18}]}'
.EE
.PP
Rename only if the name is unchanged:
.IP
.EX
qt cas users a3f10c2b '{"condition": {"column": "name", "op": "=",
	"value": "ann"}, "setCols": {"name": "anna"}}'
.EE
.PP
Average age of users that are active or have no status:
.IP
.EX
qt query users '{"aggregate": "age", "or": [
	[{"column": "active", "op": "=", "value": true}],
	[{"column": "status", "op": "MISSING"}]]}'
.EE
.PP
Delete inactive users, at most 1000 at a time:
.IP
.EX
qt del-query users '{"limit": 1000,
	"where": [{"column": "active", "op": "=", "value": false}]}'
.EE
.PP
Talk to another server:
.IP
.EX
QUICKTABLE_ADDR=http://db:16000 QUICKTABLE_TOKEN=$(cat ~/.qt-token) qt list-tables
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B cmd/client
.br
.B pkg/client
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR quicktable (1),
.I docs/rest.md
for the REST API and the operators accepted in
.BR where ,
.B or
and
.B cas
and
.B cad
conditions.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status is 0 on success,
1 if the request failed or the server returned an error,
reported as
.B "error: quicktable: \fIstatus message\fP" ,
and 2 on a usage error.
